1
00:00:02,480 --> 00:00:03,360
Hey, Yui!

2
00:00:03,640 --> 00:00:04,934
See if this will work!

3
00:00:06,680 --> 00:00:08,320
I'm transferring the code!

4
00:00:09,060 --> 00:00:10,295
We're gonna teleport!

5
00:00:10,480 --> 00:00:11,951
Daddy, give me your hand!

6
00:00:19,380 --> 00:00:20,460
Daddy! Daddy!

7
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:24,700
Yui, where are we?

8
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:26,330
I don't know.

9
00:00:26,413 --> 00:00:27,917
There's no mapping data available.

10
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:31,300
Then do you know where Asuna is? Yes.

11
00:00:32,640 --> 00:00:33,660
She's close.

12
00:00:33,940 --> 00:00:35,160
Very close, in fact.

13
00:00:36,660 --> 00:00:37,540
This way!

14
00:01:07,140 --> 00:01:08,280
Is this it?

15
00:01:08,560 --> 00:01:10,700
Is this the top of the world tree?

16
00:01:13,160 --> 00:01:15,925
There's supposed to be
a floating city up here.

17
00:01:16,940 --> 00:01:18,940
There was never any grand quest.

18
00:01:19,220 --> 00:01:21,044
The whole damn thing was a lie.

19
00:01:21,140 --> 00:01:22,580
He's gonna pay for this.

20
00:01:24,560 --> 00:01:25,677
Yeah, I know.

21
00:01:25,760 --> 00:01:29,140
So, we got to get Asuna out
of here first, right? Mm-hmm.

22
00:01:57,080 --> 00:01:59,360
I'll have a big true desire.

23
00:02:12,760 --> 00:02:17,160
It's just a miracle that I don't know,

24
00:02:17,700 --> 00:02:19,840
I'll keep it in the dark.

25
00:02:38,860 --> 00:02:39,690
Thank you

26
00:02:39,773 --> 00:02:46,580
so

27
00:02:49,120 --> 00:02:50,179
much for watching.

28
00:03:34,320 --> 00:03:35,720
Mama!

29
00:03:38,440 --> 00:03:39,840
Mama!

30
00:03:41,460 --> 00:03:42,860
Mama!

31
00:03:49,840 --> 00:03:51,120
Mommy!

32
00:03:52,280 --> 00:03:53,680
Yui!

33
00:03:54,260 --> 00:03:55,660
Mommy!

34
00:03:56,380 --> 00:03:57,480
Yui!

35
00:04:00,160 --> 00:04:01,560
Mommy!

36
00:04:02,420 --> 00:04:03,250
Mommy!

37
00:04:15,960 --> 00:04:17,360
Kirito...

38
00:04:19,440 --> 00:04:20,270
Asuna.

39
00:04:25,560 --> 00:04:27,920
Hey, sorry I took so long.

40
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:30,760
No, it's okay. Really.

41
00:04:31,220 --> 00:04:33,160
I always knew you'd save me.

42
00:04:39,020 --> 00:04:40,960
Well, ready to go home?

43
00:04:43,900 --> 00:04:44,860
Hey, Yui.

44
00:04:45,240 --> 00:04:47,122
Can you log Asuna out from here?

45
00:04:47,360 --> 00:04:48,360
Uh-uh.

46
00:04:48,820 --> 00:04:52,497
Her status is locked by complicated
codes that I don't have access to.

47
00:04:52,580 --> 00:04:55,397
We'll need to find a system
console to bypass them.

48
00:04:55,480 --> 00:04:58,140
I found a console in
the laboratory. I can...

49
00:05:01,580 --> 00:05:02,410
What's that?

50
00:05:08,900 --> 00:05:10,520
Ewing, what's happening?

51
00:05:13,200 --> 00:05:15,420
Daddy! Mommy!

52
00:05:15,840 --> 00:05:17,997
Be careful! Something...

53
00:05:18,080 --> 00:05:19,720
something bad's coming!

54
00:05:21,060 --> 00:05:21,890
Julie!

55
00:05:27,520 --> 00:05:28,860
Asuna!

56
00:05:38,200 --> 00:05:39,600
What a surprise.

57
00:05:40,300 --> 00:05:44,900
The last thing I expected to find was
a cockroach in my little bird's cage.

58
00:05:45,300 --> 00:05:47,800
You've got to be kidding! It's Sugou!

59
00:05:49,380 --> 00:05:50,380
Mama.

60
00:05:50,720 --> 00:05:53,717
I'd prefer it if you didn't
call me that name in this world.

61
00:05:53,800 --> 00:05:57,640
You should address me as His
Highness, the Fairy King Oberon!

62
00:05:59,340 --> 00:06:00,170
Kirito!

63
00:06:00,700 --> 00:06:02,000
How do you like it?

64
00:06:02,300 --> 00:06:04,017
Wanna know why you can't move?

65
00:06:04,100 --> 00:06:08,197
It's a little something called gravity
magic coming out in the next update.

66
00:06:08,280 --> 00:06:10,117
You think the players will go for it?

67
00:06:10,200 --> 00:06:12,340
Leave him alone, you coward!

68
00:06:12,960 --> 00:06:14,780
Tell me something, Kirigaya.

69
00:06:15,200 --> 00:06:17,780
Or should I call you Kirito instead?

70
00:06:18,640 --> 00:06:21,480
How did you manage to
get all the way up here?

71
00:06:22,200 --> 00:06:25,220
I saw a strange program
running, is that how?

72
00:06:25,920 --> 00:06:28,720
I flew up here with my wings!

73
00:06:29,660 --> 00:06:31,000
Ha! Suit yourself.

74
00:06:31,540 --> 00:06:33,657
If you don't want to tell me, that's fine.

75
00:06:33,740 --> 00:06:36,660
I'll just go ask your mind instead. What?

76
00:06:37,200 --> 00:06:38,220
Oh, please.

77
00:06:38,600 --> 00:06:40,657
You don't really think I went to all that

78
00:06:40,740 --> 00:06:43,297
trouble setting this whole
thing up just for fun,

79
00:06:43,380 --> 00:06:44,210
did you?

80
00:06:44,800 --> 00:06:48,437
I have 300 former players
of SAO under my thumb,

81
00:06:48,520 --> 00:06:51,226
and now thanks to their
dedicated cooperation,

82
00:06:51,700 --> 00:06:54,077
The technology I developed
for total control

83
00:06:54,160 --> 00:06:56,720
of emotions and thought is 80 % complete.

84
00:06:57,520 --> 00:06:59,877
I'm about to achieve what no one else has.

85
00:06:59,960 --> 00:07:02,320
The total control of the human soul.

86
00:07:02,580 --> 00:07:03,698
The power of a god.

87
00:07:03,900 --> 00:07:06,080
It's so close I can almost taste it.

88
00:07:06,560 --> 00:07:09,266
Seriously, thank god for
virtual reality, huh?

89
00:07:13,640 --> 00:07:14,470
Sugou!

90
00:07:14,820 --> 00:07:17,257
You're never going to get
away with this, you hear?

91
00:07:17,340 --> 00:07:18,240
You monster!

92
00:07:19,040 --> 00:07:21,357
And who do you think's going to stop me?

93
00:07:21,440 --> 00:07:22,640
Oh, maybe a god.

94
00:07:22,900 --> 00:07:25,017
But sadly, there's none in this world.

95
00:07:25,100 --> 00:07:26,660
Except for yours truly!

96
00:07:28,360 --> 00:07:29,240
I know!

97
00:07:29,580 --> 00:07:32,097
Before I start tinkering
with your little souls,

98
00:07:32,180 --> 00:07:34,592
why don't we have ourselves a little fun?

99
00:07:44,120 --> 00:07:45,240
You bastard!

100
00:07:45,660 --> 00:07:46,700
Leave her alone!

101
00:08:05,580 --> 00:08:06,410
Yes!

102
00:08:09,540 --> 00:08:10,370
Great!

103
00:08:11,720 --> 00:08:13,337
That's what I was hoping for.

104
00:08:13,420 --> 00:08:16,244
You can't get NPC girls
to make faces like that.

105
00:08:20,180 --> 00:08:22,160
Ah, you smell lovely.

106
00:08:22,940 --> 00:08:27,469
Figuring out how to replicate the way
you smell in real life was a challenge.

107
00:08:28,040 --> 00:08:31,517
And don't even get me
started on how hard it was to

108
00:08:31,600 --> 00:08:34,700
get an analyzer into your
hospital room undetected.

109
00:08:35,620 --> 00:08:37,000
Get away from her!

110
00:08:37,780 --> 00:08:38,840
She's so cool!

111
00:08:42,780 --> 00:08:44,377
Give me a break.

112
00:08:44,460 --> 00:08:48,580
Why don't you stay down and
grovel like a good little doggy?

113
00:08:58,740 --> 00:09:03,580
System command, chase the pain
absorber from level 10 to level 8.

114
00:09:08,200 --> 00:09:09,340
Hurts, doesn't it?

115
00:09:09,660 --> 00:09:13,657
I'll increase the pain gradually to
give you something to look forward to.

116
00:09:13,740 --> 00:09:14,780
By the way,

117
00:09:15,200 --> 00:09:20,017
once it drops below level three, it'll
start affecting your body in the real world.

118
00:09:20,100 --> 00:09:21,360
As for you.

119
00:09:26,100 --> 00:09:27,080
Stop it!

120
00:09:28,100 --> 00:09:28,930
Sugou!

121
00:09:29,300 --> 00:09:30,920
It's okay, Kirito.

122
00:09:31,420 --> 00:09:34,080
Whatever he does, he's
not really hurting me.

123
00:09:35,820 --> 00:09:40,420
I was hoping you'd say that, but I wonder
how long your pride's going to last.

124
00:09:40,660 --> 00:09:42,440
30 minutes? An hour?

125
00:09:43,040 --> 00:09:46,200
Why don't we see how long
you can hang on to it?

126
00:10:03,560 --> 00:10:07,854
Now that that's out of the way, would
you like to know what I'm thinking?

127
00:10:07,940 --> 00:10:12,700
Once we've had our fun here, I'm going
to pay you a visit at the hospital.

128
00:10:13,460 --> 00:10:16,437
I'll set up a big monitor
and play back a recording

129
00:10:16,520 --> 00:10:20,197
of this and we can enjoy
ourselves all over again,

130
00:10:20,280 --> 00:10:24,680
but this time with your real body.

131
00:10:38,160 --> 00:10:40,560
Yummy, how sweet.

132
00:10:41,620 --> 00:10:43,560
Go, you bastard!

133
00:10:44,120 --> 00:10:45,760
You bastard! Run!

134
00:10:54,140 --> 00:10:56,280
I'll kill you! You hear?

135
00:10:56,660 --> 00:10:58,480
I'm gonna kill you!

136
00:11:12,220 --> 00:11:14,060
Why is this happening?

137
00:11:15,440 --> 00:11:18,900
Am I being punished for thinking
I was some kind of hero?

138
00:11:19,560 --> 00:11:23,040
For thinking I was the only
one who could save Asuna?

139
00:11:23,940 --> 00:11:27,960
For thinking I was strong
enough, even though I'm not?

140
00:11:33,960 --> 00:11:35,440
Are you giving up?

141
00:11:38,200 --> 00:11:39,640
Are you giving up?

142
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:41,830
No.

143
00:11:41,913 --> 00:11:43,437
I'm facing reality.

144
00:11:43,520 --> 00:11:48,260
Then you are giving up to the
power of a system you once defied.

145
00:11:49,220 --> 00:11:50,900
What choice do I have?

146
00:11:51,160 --> 00:11:52,580
I'm just a player.

147
00:11:52,920 --> 00:11:54,440
And he's the GM.

148
00:11:55,280 --> 00:11:58,340
Then our battle was... what? A joke?

149
00:11:59,160 --> 00:12:01,577
Do you remember how
you showed me the power

150
00:12:01,660 --> 00:12:04,307
of the human will was
superior to the system?

151
00:12:04,560 --> 00:12:07,501
How you showed me the
possibilities of the future?

152
00:12:08,100 --> 00:12:08,930
You're...

153
00:12:10,680 --> 00:12:13,460
Get up, Kirito. Get up!

154
00:12:26,960 --> 00:12:29,380
Your attacks are weak.

155
00:12:30,520 --> 00:12:33,100
The blades in SAO hit way harder.

156
00:12:34,660 --> 00:12:36,820
And they hurt way more.

157
00:12:44,560 --> 00:12:45,420
Unbelievable.

158
00:12:46,220 --> 00:12:48,600
I've got a few bugs left to deal with.

159
00:12:50,860 --> 00:12:52,360
System login.

160
00:12:53,060 --> 00:12:55,840
ID Heathcliff. What?

161
00:12:56,800 --> 00:12:58,680
Whose ID are you using?

162
00:12:58,980 --> 00:13:00,040
System command.

163
00:13:00,360 --> 00:13:02,242
Enable administrator privileges.

164
00:13:02,940 --> 00:13:04,900
Set ID Oberon to level one.

165
00:13:07,260 --> 00:13:09,160
An ID that outranks mine?

166
00:13:09,780 --> 00:13:10,860
That's impossible!

167
00:13:11,220 --> 00:13:13,320
This is my world. I'm the creator.

168
00:13:13,600 --> 00:13:16,060
I'm its ruler, its king, its god!

169
00:13:16,180 --> 00:13:17,420
No, I don't think so.

170
00:13:17,960 --> 00:13:20,160
You stole everything in this world.

171
00:13:20,420 --> 00:13:22,480
Everything, including its people.

172
00:13:22,760 --> 00:13:27,113
You're nothing but a king of thieves,
sitting alone on your stolen throne.

173
00:13:27,320 --> 00:13:28,720
You little punk.

174
00:13:29,280 --> 00:13:30,340
You dare?

175
00:13:30,580 --> 00:13:32,600
You dare talk to me like that?

176
00:13:33,620 --> 00:13:34,660
System command!

177
00:13:34,900 --> 00:13:36,140
Generate Object!

178
00:13:36,480 --> 00:13:38,120
ID Excalibur!

179
00:13:39,980 --> 00:13:42,740
Do as I say, you piece of crap!

180
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:45,800
System, your God is
ordering you to comply!

181
00:13:46,740 --> 00:13:48,677
Think you can wait a little bit longer?

182
00:13:48,760 --> 00:13:50,340
This will only take a sec.

183
00:13:54,720 --> 00:13:55,777
System Command!

184
00:13:55,860 --> 00:13:56,980
Generate Object!

185
00:13:57,480 --> 00:13:59,280
ID Excalibur!

186
00:14:01,060 --> 00:14:04,900
A simple command summons a
legendary weapon. Who knew?

187
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:16,220
It's time to settle the score.

188
00:14:16,660 --> 00:14:19,880
The King of Thieves
versus the Gilded Hero.

189
00:14:21,060 --> 00:14:24,420
System command, set Pain Absorber to zero.

190
00:14:25,660 --> 00:14:27,300
No, not that. What?

191
00:14:27,460 --> 00:14:28,820
Did you just flinch?

192
00:14:29,020 --> 00:14:32,877
Because the other guy never flinched,
no matter how bad things got.

193
00:14:32,960 --> 00:14:33,790
You know him.

194
00:14:34,140 --> 00:14:35,220
Akihiko Kayaba!

195
00:14:35,520 --> 00:14:36,760
Oh my god.

196
00:14:37,700 --> 00:14:38,530
Kayaba?

197
00:14:38,700 --> 00:14:39,680
Oh, I get it.

198
00:14:39,820 --> 00:14:40,960
That was his ID.

199
00:14:41,540 --> 00:14:42,370
Why?

200
00:14:42,520 --> 00:14:44,108
You're supposed to be dead.

201
00:14:44,280 --> 00:14:46,237
Why are you still getting in my way?

202
00:14:46,320 --> 00:14:48,300
You are always doing this!

203
00:14:48,580 --> 00:14:51,345
Acting all high and
mighty, like some big shot!

204
00:14:51,480 --> 00:14:53,597
Taking everything that
was rightfully mine!

205
00:14:53,680 --> 00:14:56,717
Sugo, in a way, I get
where you're coming from.

206
00:14:56,800 --> 00:15:00,217
I lost to him too, and
then I had to go work for,

207
00:15:00,300 --> 00:15:07,120
but whatever happened, I never
wanted to be him, unlike you.

208
00:15:07,940 --> 00:15:08,840
Damn you!

209
00:15:26,540 --> 00:15:28,720
It hurts, doesn't it?

210
00:15:29,200 --> 00:15:32,280
But it's nothing like the
pain you made Asuna feel.

211
00:15:32,540 --> 00:15:33,560
Not even close!

212
00:15:39,860 --> 00:15:41,060
My hand!

213
00:15:41,300 --> 00:15:43,100
My hand! My hand!

214
00:15:58,140 --> 00:16:01,000
Oh, my God.

215
00:16:34,940 --> 00:16:36,760
I had faith in you.

216
00:16:37,460 --> 00:16:39,360
I have faith in you.

217
00:16:40,120 --> 00:16:41,840
Always have, always will.

218
00:16:42,220 --> 00:16:44,540
And I know you'll always save me.

219
00:16:44,900 --> 00:16:46,620
Because you're my hero.

220
00:16:48,060 --> 00:16:50,340
I don't have any power.

221
00:16:50,860 --> 00:16:52,400
I'm not a hero.

222
00:16:57,820 --> 00:17:00,660
But I'll do my best to be one.

223
00:17:04,260 --> 00:17:06,040
Come on, let's go home.

224
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:11,588
It's got to be nighttime
already back there.

225
00:17:11,860 --> 00:17:14,801
But I'll see you at the
hospital as soon as I can.

226
00:17:15,100 --> 00:17:16,512
I'll be waiting for you.

227
00:17:16,760 --> 00:17:19,995
I want you to be the first
person I see when I wake up.

228
00:17:22,540 --> 00:17:24,417
It's finally over, isn't it?

229
00:17:24,500 --> 00:17:30,160
We're going home back to the
real world, that's right.

230
00:17:31,080 --> 00:17:33,737
But a lot's changed, so
try not to freak out.

231
00:17:33,820 --> 00:17:37,077
Let's go places and do fun things.

232
00:17:37,160 --> 00:17:40,797
Just the two of us—sound
good, yeah, real good.

233
00:17:40,880 --> 00:17:41,710
That's

234
00:18:09,360 --> 00:18:13,777
it, game over, or is it?

235
00:18:13,860 --> 00:18:17,117
What do you think, Heathcliff?

236
00:18:17,200 --> 00:18:18,320
heathcliff

237
00:18:20,320 --> 00:18:22,680
Good to see you again, Kirito.

238
00:18:23,080 --> 00:18:24,420
So you are alive.

239
00:18:24,940 --> 00:18:27,460
You could say I'm alive, in a way.

240
00:18:28,480 --> 00:18:32,421
Ultimately, I'm the afterimage of
the mind that was Akihiko Kayaba.

241
00:18:32,900 --> 00:18:33,840
An echo.

242
00:18:34,380 --> 00:18:37,700
And, as usual, I have no idea
what you're talking about.

243
00:18:38,020 --> 00:18:40,079
I guess I should thank you, though.

244
00:18:40,840 --> 00:18:42,120
That's not necessary.

245
00:18:42,520 --> 00:18:43,520
What do you mean?

246
00:18:43,720 --> 00:18:47,757
We're not exactly friends, so we
shouldn't expect favors from each other.

247
00:18:47,840 --> 00:18:49,193
There's always a price.

248
00:18:50,400 --> 00:18:52,694
Always okay, what do you want me to do?

249
00:19:02,460 --> 00:19:06,037
What's this—the beginnings of a
new world, I call it the seed?

250
00:19:06,120 --> 00:19:06,950
Once

251
00:19:08,400 --> 00:19:12,777
it sprouts, you'll know what it is;
what you do with it is up to you.

252
00:19:12,860 --> 00:19:14,657
You can even delete it if?

253
00:19:14,740 --> 00:19:15,570
if

254
00:19:16,560 --> 00:19:20,537
However, if you still have a tiny bit
of fondness left for the virtual world,

255
00:19:20,620 --> 00:19:21,973
you'll take care of it.

256
00:19:24,860 --> 00:19:26,300
I should get going now.

257
00:19:26,740 --> 00:19:29,080
I do hope we meet again, Kirito.

258
00:19:37,120 --> 00:19:37,950
Yui!

259
00:19:38,033 --> 00:19:39,940
Are you okay? Where are you?

260
00:19:42,020 --> 00:19:42,940
Thank God.

261
00:19:43,300 --> 00:19:44,140
You're safe.

262
00:19:45,420 --> 00:19:46,250
Uh-huh.

263
00:19:46,333 --> 00:19:49,309
I hid myself inside the local
memory of your nerve gear rig.

264
00:19:49,520 --> 00:19:52,180
Where's Mommy? Don't worry. She's safe.

265
00:19:52,660 --> 00:19:53,900
She's back home now.

266
00:19:54,240 --> 00:19:55,100
Mommy's back?

267
00:19:55,920 --> 00:19:57,000
Thank goodness.

268
00:19:57,440 --> 00:19:59,620
I'm so happy. Really.

269
00:20:00,280 --> 00:20:02,620
I promise we'll be back to visit soon.

270
00:20:03,540 --> 00:20:06,937
Although, I don't know how much longer
this world's going to be around.

271
00:20:07,020 --> 00:20:10,897
It doesn't matter because my core
program's inside your nerve gear now.

272
00:20:10,980 --> 00:20:12,627
So we'll always be together.

273
00:20:13,740 --> 00:20:15,560
All right. I better head out.

274
00:20:15,800 --> 00:20:17,329
I'm going to go see Mommy.

275
00:20:18,760 --> 00:20:19,590
Okay, Daddy.

276
00:20:19,673 --> 00:20:20,503
I love you.

277
00:20:47,060 --> 00:20:47,890
I'm sorry!

278
00:20:48,300 --> 00:20:52,065
When you didn't log out right
away, I got worried, and then I...

279
00:20:52,980 --> 00:20:54,980
Sorry I took so long to come back.

280
00:20:55,580 --> 00:20:57,140
Is it really over now?

281
00:20:57,540 --> 00:20:59,220
Yeah, it is.

282
00:20:59,860 --> 00:21:00,900
It's all over.

283
00:21:02,320 --> 00:21:03,240
That's awesome!

284
00:21:06,860 --> 00:21:07,760
Hey, Sugu.

285
00:21:08,340 --> 00:21:10,634
Thank you for all the help you gave me.

286
00:21:10,980 --> 00:21:12,980
I couldn't have done it on my own.

287
00:21:13,140 --> 00:21:15,077
You're the reason I was able to finish it.

288
00:21:15,160 --> 00:21:15,990
No.

289
00:21:20,060 --> 00:21:22,217
You don't have to thank me for a thing.

290
00:21:22,300 --> 00:21:26,300
I'm just happy I got the chance to
help my big brother in his world.

291
00:21:34,220 --> 00:21:35,691
What happened with Asuna?

292
00:21:36,120 --> 00:21:38,100
Did you get her back? Uh-huh.

293
00:21:38,620 --> 00:21:39,450
Finally.

294
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:41,720
She's back in the real world.

295
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:44,920
Sugu, I, uh... Uh-uh.

296
00:21:45,200 --> 00:21:46,080
You get going.

297
00:21:46,880 --> 00:21:49,704
She's gotta be wondering
where you're at by now.

298
00:21:56,800 --> 00:21:58,220
Oh, it's cold.

299
00:21:59,460 --> 00:22:00,500
Look, snow.

300
00:22:03,860 --> 00:22:05,200
Be careful out there.

301
00:22:05,460 --> 00:22:07,917
And say hi to Asuna for me. You got it.

302
00:22:08,000 --> 00:22:10,529
I can't wait for you
guys to meet for real.

303
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:04,100
Thank you.

304
00:23:35,900 --> 00:23:36,837
Next time.

305
00:23:36,920 --> 00:23:38,820
The World Seed.
